      },
      "message": "feat(ui): each setup owns its WCS, Stock, Machine, Post, Fixtures and Tool list in the browser\n\nThe browser's Setup section shows one node per setup with a radio for\nthe active setup (ActivateSetup, undoable) and its own children: WCS,\nStock, Machine, Post, Fixtures (each fixture a child), Tool list and\nOperations (1+n, machining order). A document without setups shows the\nsame children for its implicit setup. Clicking a node activates its\nsetup first, then opens its page, so no editor changes a setup the node\ndoes not belong to.\n\nA setup may own its machine and post (SetupDef.machine / .post, None =\nfollow the document's): new undoable SetSetupMachine / SetSetupPost, a\ndatum transfer carries the mount, project v55 (v54 files open\nunchanged). The app mounts the active setup's machine and post; work\ncrossing mounts is refused by name (generating an op of a setup on other\nsteel, posting a program whose setups disagree). Tool list is the\ndocument library filtered per setup (decision (b)).\n\nThe browser code moved out of panes.rs (browser_tree, browser_pane,\ntree_menu), tree glyphs out of painted.rs; decisions in\ndocs/decisions/343-setup-tree.md. Follow-ups: #388, #389.\n\nFixes #343\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
